INT. ROLLER RINK - SNACK BAR - NIGHT

Disco ball scatters light. Neon trim. Under the music, wheels rumble on wood.

PAZ ORTEGA-WILLIAMS, 17, in rental skates, leans on the counter. Her best friend, KIRA SINGH, 17, steals fries from her basket. DEWEY LAMBERT, 18, behind the counter in a paper hat, wipes it down. At a nearby table, BEATRICE "BEE" HOLLOWAY, 16, sketches in a notebook, and her brother, ARLO HOLLOWAY, 14, sips a slushie.

PAZ
Okay, but if I ask him and he says no, I have to move to another state.

KIRA
You are not moving to another state.

PAZ
Then I'm dying. Those are the options.

KIRA
He's right there. Dewey. Dewey!

DEWEY
Hey. Sorry. I was in the fryer zone.

PAZ
(low, to Kira)
Kill me.

KIRA
(to Dewey)
She wants to know if you're going to the thing on Saturday.

DEWEY
The thing?

PAZ
The thing. At the quarry.

DEWEY
Oh. The quarry. Yeah, probably. Maybe. Why?

PAZ
No reason. Just curious.

KIRA
She has a reason.

PAZ
I do not.

Dewey leans his elbows on the counter. Kira bounces on her skates. Bee tears a page from her notebook and slides it across the table to Arlo, who pockets it.

A TALL STRANGER, 20s, in a leather jacket and black skates, glides up behind Paz and taps her shoulder. This is MAXIMILIAN "MAX" DUBOIS. Paz turns. Her face does something complicated.

MAX
Paz. You never called.

PAZ
Max. I was going to.

KIRA
(under her breath)
Oh no.

DEWEY
Who's this?

MAX
Her ex.

DEWEY
Oh.

PAZ
He's not my ex. We went out twice. Once. Once and a half.

MAX
You left in the middle of the second one.

PAZ
I was sick.

MAX
You were laughing.

Bee smiles into her slushie. Arlo whispers to her. Dewey slowly picks up a rag and starts wiping the counter again, harder. Kira looks from one face to another, delighted and horrified.

KIRA
Anyone want fries?
